 "_comment": "Fake but representative data used only in discovery role-play. Never imported by development/. Shapes mirror what the live storefront-frontend receives: OrderServices.getStockSummary({catalogueType}) -> {data:{products:[...]}} and ProductBatch.list() -> [...]. A product's batchStock[] cross-references batches[] by batchId, which is exactly how InventoryHealth joins expiry dates onto live stock.",
 "_source": "Ported from storefront-frontend@develop -- src/pages/Inventory.jsx (/inventory) and src/pages/RawMaterialsInventory.jsx (/raw-material-inventory). See discovery/instructions/addendum-002-live-inventory-port.md.",
 "_dateComment": "Batch dates are stored as OFFSETS (createdDaysAgo, mfgDaysAgo, expiryInDays) and resolved to real dates at load time. Live the API returns absolute ISO dates; offsets are used here so the expired / near-expiry (<=30d) / healthy buckets stay correct however long after freezing this prototype is opened. A negative expiryInDays is already-expired.",
